# Brainfuck native AArch64 wide slot streaming stage
# Input is the filtered source stream terminated by zero
# Every accepted instruction emits twelve machine words
# Bracket slots have unconditional branches with unset targets
# Counts are held as three unsigned bytes in little endian order
# End output is count then a zero terminator and status byte
# Status one denotes an invalid instruction
# Status two denotes an overflowing command count
# Status three denotes bracket slots needing relocation
# The current stage does not construct a complete ELF file
